{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792753794,"nonce":"Dbd2gMqVfqbEOUu51Dgizx2PZQw=","title":"Execute implicit abstract conversions in macro helper calls","message":"RayDE inline markup now reaches ashui.ui.Hxx.hxx after traversing the @:pos metadata returned by ashui.ui.Markup.build, but its actual macro interpreter execution fails with `Expr has no field 'source'`. tink.hxx.Parser.parseRootWith passes an Expr to the local `create(source:ParserSource)` callback. ParserSource is an abstract whose @:from fromExpr converts the expression to `{source, offset, fileName}`. The AST interpreter binds callback arguments without running that conversion and ClassRegistry registers executable bodies only for classes.\n\nReproducer: from the RayDE workspace, typecheck an in-memory source `@:build(ashui.ui.Markup.build()) class MacroDslProbe { public static function main() { var box = \u003cdiv/\u003e; var node = box.node; } }`. No on-disk RayDE changes are needed. `cargo test -p rayzor-lsp --lib rayde_markup_reaches_the_generated_div_type --offline -- --ignored --nocapture` preserves the acceptance test. Failure log: /tmp/rayzor-real-dsl3.log. The required result is a Div local type, a final expansion rather than Hxx.hxx, and no macro error.\n\nImplement general macro-time abstract @:from conversion and abstract helper dispatch using declared argument types, including local closures, static methods, constructors and instance methods. Preserve declaration/import context and report conversion failures. Do not special-case ashui or infer a tag type from its spelling. Follow the real expansion after conversion: tink also uses abstract StringSlice, inherited ParserBase methods, regex operations and string methods; inspect each newly exposed operation rather than hiding failures with Dynamic.\n\nThe Expr-versus-String false diagnostic is a separate runtime-signature projection issue. Fixing it does not complete this interpreter work.","files":null}]}